Spec: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/spec.md (Anthropic parser: Events, Tolerance, Per-exchange status; AC11, AC35, AC36, AC48)
Research: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/research.md Q2 (block names), Q8 (synthetic non_streaming and error fixtures)
Why this approach: the 2xx body is read token by token with json.Decoder, so a cut body keeps role, stop_reason and each whole content block before the cut, and the same code path serves complete bodies; blocks go through T20's mapBlock with source response. A streamed response (ParseInput.Stream) is left to T22. Usage keeps the four counters and puts every other usage key in detail, so T22 can merge message_start and message_delta keys into the same shape. Details recorded in plan.md ("Details fixed in T21").
Alternatives rejected: a whole-body json.Unmarshal with no tolerant pass (a truncated body would yield nothing); salvaging a truncated request body (T20's plan decision keeps it partial with no request events); treating a non-envelope error body as ok (the spec keeps failed for a malformed body that isn't truncated).
Trade-off / known limit: a non-2xx HTML body from a proxy is parse failed with a capture_failed line, though its error event (status only) is stored. TestParse_NonStreaming compares with a golden file until T22 adds the streamed equivalent; the non_streaming fixture holds a text block and a tool_use, so T22 needs a matching stream built for it. The stream_error.sse fixture is committed but only used from T22.
Verified by: make verify. Tests first failed for the right reason: TestParse_NonStreaming (only request events), TestParse_UpstreamError/status_429 (no error event), TestParse_FailureKeepsRaw/response (parse ok, no capture_failed), TestCapture_BodyOverCapTruncated/non_streamed_json_parses_partial (no response blocks kept). Also added: TestParse_TruncatedJSONResponse, TestParse_UpstreamErrorBodyUnreadable (html, truncated, empty), TestParse_StreamedResponseNotReadAsJSON. TestFixtures_NoIdentifiers passes over the new fixtures.
